  "question": {
    "text": "A sphere of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;moving with velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> collides head-on with another sphere of the same mass at rest. If the coefficient of restitution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, then what is the ratio of final velocity of the second sphere to the initial velocity of the first sphere?",
